  "description": "CAXDUC crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C42 H104 Dy5 N6 O28 9+,9(Cl1 1-),24(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.710-3.872 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 103.57-109.87°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy5(μ3-OH)6(Acc)6(H2O)10]·Cl9·24H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 10 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
